From 6253b8525e8d4a137f355373a352c70fdd7aecd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:38:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Managed pin gate judges bare custom/empty providers
 as the turn does

Five whys: (1) A pick the picker offered or session.create accepted still killed
the chat's first turn with ManagedPinRejectedError. (2) For a bare `custom` or
empty provider the turn re-derives the provider (canonical_custom_identity /
empty_provider_identity) before pin_policy; the gate did not, and accepted
whenever any route named the model (_REDERIVED_PROVIDERS early return).
(3) The re-derivation lived inline in tui_gateway.agent_factory
._resolve_agent_model_runtime, so the gate could not call it. (4) Two
copies of "which provider does this pin run on" can only drift. (5) No test
compared the gate to the turn on the stored override.

Countermeasure: one public derivation,
hermes_cli.runtime_provider_custom.rederived_override_provider, used by
_resolve_agent_model_runtime (behaviour unchanged) and by
model_options_managed._refusal, which drops _REDERIVED_PROVIDERS and judges
every non-class pin as pin_policy(model, rederived provider). Reviewer probes now
refused at session.create (-32602): anthropic-deep on `custom` (stock registry),
anthropic-deep registered on two levels / two providers with no provider.

Proof:
- RED on 187108567cfa: 11 new tests fail (5 in test_model_options_managed_pins,
  6 in test_session_create_managed_pin_guard); GREEN after: 38 pass in the two files.
- Mutation (old early accept for ""/custom restored): 11 fail (5 + 6).
- Agreement test: concrete/auto/""/custom x (allowed, unregistered, ambiguous):
  gate refuses iff _resolve_agent_model_runtime raises ManagedPinRejectedError.
- Reviewer's 4 files + 7 derivation suites (11 files): 817 passed.
- scripts/check --base origin/main: ok.
